Z||000000||d825077||03-11-2000||10:23 AM||||When I bought my 88 4 cylinder Fiero the rear tires were unevenly worn.  The inside of both of them were wearing faster than the rest of the tire.  I replaced both tires and had the car alinged.  A couple of months latter I noticed the same problem.  When ever I go around a turn the tires also screech.  Do you think I need new struts or is it something esle?  Thank you.||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||03-11-2000||11:28 AM||||my guess would be struts... but that is just a guess ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||03-11-2000||12:24 PM||||Have it checked for negative camber. I posted in a similar thread started by 87EC05 in the off topic section earlier this week. There may be some helpful information there too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||03-11-2000||09:55 PM||||Tires usually get cupped with bad struts. Inside wear often indicates poor alignment.||||reg||1
